[h1]🇺🇦 Barony Ukrainian Localization[/h1]
[i]Game version: v5.0.2[/i]

A complete Ukrainian localization of Barony: the interface, dialogues, items, descriptions, names and most other in-game text are translated.

[b]How to enable it:[/b]
[list]
[*]Launch Barony on Steam
[*]Choose [b]Play Modded Game[/b]
[*]Pick [b]«Українізатор»[/b] in the list of mods
[/list]

[b]Important: if the game does not start or crashes on launch[/b], check this file:

[code]/Books/compiled_books.json[/code]

Try deleting it, restoring the original file, or setting its [b]Read-only[/b] attribute. See the details below.

[h2]Alternative installation[/h2]

The localization can also be installed directly into the game files.

Open the mod folder:

[code]Steam\steamapps\workshop\content\371970\3711160804[/code]

Copy everything from it into the folder where Barony is installed, replacing the existing files.

After that the game starts in Ukrainian right away, in the normal mode — no need to pick [b]Play Modded Game[/b] and the [b]«Українізатор»[/b] mod every time.

[i]Back up the original game files before replacing them. Verifying the game files through Steam may restore the originals and undo the changes.[/i]

[h2]Features[/h2]
[list]
[*]Interface, dialogues, items, names, descriptions and other text are translated
[*]Compendium entries are translated
[*]Maximum coverage of the game's text
[*]Text baked into the maps and a few game-specific elements are not translated
[*]The translation is machine-made and has not been fully proofread by hand
[/list]

[h2]Known issues[/h2]

[b]Possible freezes[/b]
[list]
[*]Short freezes may occur while starting or loading the game
[*]The likely cause is the fonts with an extended character set, which the game was not optimized for
[/list]

[b]The compiled_books.json problem[/b]
[list]
[*]Affected file: [code]/Books/compiled_books.json[/code]
[*]The game writes the translation into it but does not always delete or restore the file on exit
[*]Because of this the next launch may end with an error
[/list]

[b]Possible fixes:[/b]
[list]
[*]Delete [code]/Books/compiled_books.json[/code]
[*]Restore its original version
[*]Set the file's [b]Read-only[/b] attribute
[/list]

[i]Note: verifying or restoring the game files may reset the Read-only attribute.[/i]

[b]Garbled characters[/b]
[list]
[*]Mojibake or other broken characters may appear in some places
[*]These will be fixed gradually in future updates of the localization
[/list]

[b]Untranslated text on maps[/b]
[list]
[*]Some text is stored directly in the map files
[*]Such elements cannot be translated with the standard localization tools
[/list]

[h2]Additional notes[/h2]

This is a machine translation, so the text may contain mistakes, inaccuracies or awkward wording. That said, in my opinion the overall quality is good enough for a comfortable playthrough.

If you find mistakes, inaccuracies, broken characters or untranslated lines — please report them.

[h2]Project repository[/h2]

The localization files and working materials are available in the repository:

[url=https://github.com/UKA-Localization/Barony-localization-uk-UA]Barony-localization-uk-UA — GitHub[/url]

The project's name, structure or location may change in the future, so check the repository for up-to-date information.

The project will be maintained as long as players are interested in it.

If you would like to help — get in touch. Beyond this localization, translations of other games are possible in the future.

No special technical skills are required to help. Simply reading the texts and checking whether they sound natural in Ukrainian is already a useful contribution.

